 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "YUitFSTEBgAJ",
   "from": "klb...@gmail.com",
   "author": "088e8a47a714e2a7",
   "date": "2017-08-11T23:13:47Z",
   "subject": "NA values returned for estimate.missing",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><div><div><div><div style=\"overflow:auto\"><div style=\"max-height:10000px\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><br>I am using the following code to estimate missing landmarks using the TPS method:<div><br></div><div><div>H&lt;-readland.nts(&quot;Homo_MD.nts&quot;)</div><div>E&lt;-estimate.missing(H, method=&quot;TPS&quot;)</div></div><div><br></div><div>The returned value (E) contains a number of NA values, all in the position of the z coordinate for one specimen. The next specimen in the file is unaffected.</div><div><br></div><div>Anyone know why this might happen?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks, Karen</div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s1oWXHBsBwAJ",
   "from": "Emma Sherratt",
   "author": "91722721526eb1d7",
   "date": "2017-08-14T02:37:52Z",
   "subject": "Re: NA values returned for estimate.missing",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear Karen,<div><br></div><div>I suspect you have used the wrong read function for your NTS file. See here for more details: <a href=\"https://github.com/geomorphR/geomorph/wiki/Reading-NTS-files\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/geomorphR/geomorph/wiki/Reading-NTS-files&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792486065933000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3LLjvkJ_cV4t9xmjGHXZ2B\">https://github.com/geomorphR/geomorph/wiki/Reading-NTS-files</a></div><div><br></div><div>Basically, there are two file types, and if you&#39;ve used the wrong one, H will not be formatted correctly. Check the dim() of H to make sure it is a 3D array with dimensions you are expecting.</div><div><br></div><div>Emma</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div><br><br>On Saturday, 12 August 2017 08:43:47 UTC+9:30, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">klb...@gmail.com</a>  wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><br><div><div><div><div style=\"overflow:auto\"><div style=\"max-height:10000px\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><br>I am using the following code to estimate missing landmarks using the TPS method:<div><br></div><div><div>H&lt;-readland.nts(&quot;Homo_MD.nts&quot;)</div><div>E&lt;-estimate.missing(H, method=&quot;TPS&quot;)</div></div><div><br></div><div>The returned value (E) contains a number of NA values, all in the position of the z coordinate for one specimen. The next specimen in the file is unaffected.</div><div><br></div><div>Anyone know why this might happen?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks, Karen</div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
